Manage verified spec-driven development change workspaces

Usage: specsync change [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new                Create a draft change and return the deterministic interview
  answer             Answer one deterministic interview question
  depend             Declare deterministic ordering between active changes
  supersede          Adopt one exact predecessor path/module obligation before definition approval
  reconcile-history  Request explicitly unproven historical receipt reconciliation; requires fresh scope approval
  list               List active changes
  show               Show one change, its gate health, and next questions
  status             Show lifecycle status for one change or all active changes
  ship-status        Report ship readiness: tip class, trust guidance, stages, and merge risk
  pr                 Archive the change if needed, push the branch, and open or reuse the pull request
  ship               Preflight ship readiness and finalize when the change is ready
  approve            Record the mandatory definition approval
  review             Record a scoped human review of the current implementation
  reopen             Reopen stale accepted evidence for a fresh verification and closing approval
  send-back          Send an approved, implementing or verifying change back to draft for re-scoping
  correct            Correct supported accepted interview metadata through append-only audit evidence
  correct-owner      Correct one or more exact canonical owners used by accepted delivery evidence
  finalize           Finalize and archive the reviewed change on its existing pull request. Writes an archive tip for the same PR — merge only after finalize; merging first orphans verification evidence and blocks every earlier accepted change sharing a delivery input from archiving until this one is finalized
  check              Materialize approved deltas and run targeted verification for one change
  audit              Audit active change workspaces and living SDD policy/spec coherence
  adopt              Adopt the current verified lifecycle in an existing project
  help               Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --strict                     Treat warnings as errors
      --require-coverage <N>       Fail if file coverage percent is below this threshold
      --root <ROOT>                Project root directory (default: cwd)
      --format <FORMAT>            Output format: text, json, markdown, github, table, or csv [default: text] [possible values: text, json, markdown, github, table, csv]
      --json                       Output results as JSON (shorthand for --format json)
      --enforcement <MODE>         Enforcement mode: strict (default, exit 1 on errors), enforce-new (block unspecced files), warn (exit 0). Overrides the `enforcement` field in .specsync/config.toml [possible values: warn, enforce-new, strict]
      --exclude-status <STATUSES>  Exclude specs with these statuses (comma-separated, e.g. "deprecated,archived")
      --only-status <STATUSES>     Only include specs with these statuses (comma-separated, e.g. "active,stable")
